<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Cobá</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 1100 CE (approx.) · capital Cobá</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A large Maya city among lakes in north-eastern Yucatán, hub of the longest known Maya causeway network.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Cobá developed around a group of lakes in the north-east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán</a> peninsula, whose water supported a large population. It became a major centre in the Classic period, from about 600 CE, with stelae showing southern Maya influence.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>More than 50 raised white causeways (sakbeob) radiate from Cobá. One runs about 100 kilometres west to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaxuna">Yaxuná</a>, perhaps to secure control of territory against rivals in the centre of the peninsula. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nohoch-mul">Nohoch Mul</a> pyramid is among the tallest in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yucatan-peninsula">Yucatán</a>. Stelae depict rulers standing on captives, and some royal women are also recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Cobá lost power to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chichen-itza">Chichen Itza</a> in the 10th and 11th centuries and was largely abandoned by about 1100, though Postclassic shrines were later added. It is now a popular archaeological site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quintana-roo">Quintana Roo</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/coba.jpg" alt="Cobá" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: O.Mustafin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coba1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 1100 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cobá</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Coba</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=850&amp;focus=coba" aria-label="Cobá on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2317 1419 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Cobá lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2637 1675h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2637 1675h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=850&amp;focus=coba">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

